  - The exact manual test I should run, as a numbered checklist.
- **Scope discipline.** Never refactor outside the current phase. Log
  discoveries in `FOLLOWUPS.md` (append-only, one line per item:
  `- [phase N] <issue> — discovered YYYY-MM-DD`).
- **Migrations.**
  - File path: `supabase/migrations/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_short_name.sql` only. Never
    drop a loose `.sql` into `supabase/`.
  - Reversible. Include the rollback in a comment block at the top.
  - **Never destructive without explicit "yes, drop it" from me.**
  - Phase 16 ships ONE additive migration (`add_event_type_to_tournaments`).
    Phases 17–19 are designed to require zero further schema changes. If a
    migration becomes necessary outside Phase 16, stop and ask before
    authoring it.
- **Auth in new code.**
  - Admin pages: wrap in `AdminGate` or check session in a Server Component.
  - Admin API routes: call `verifyAdminSessionCookieValue` on the request cookie.
  - Player pages: use Supabase Auth helpers via `getCurrentPlayer()` and
    `createSupabaseServerClient()` / `createSupabaseBrowserClient()`. Never
    `app-signing` for player flows.
  - Server-side gating: call `supabase.auth.getUser()`, never `getSession()`.
    `getUser()` validates the JWT; `getSession()` trusts the cookie.
- **Code style.** Match existing structure. New components under
  `src/components/<area>/`. **No new top-level npm dependencies** without my
  explicit approval. Phases 16–19 are scoped to need zero new packages — every
  feature reuses the existing tournament/registration code paths plus a
  small new `PublicRoster` component.
- **TypeScript.** Strict mode. No `any` in new code. Narrow types at API
  boundaries with hand-rolled guards unless a guard already exists in the repo.
- **No emojis.** In code, comments, commit messages, or UI strings.
- **Uncertainty.** If unsure about a data model, route, or component, ask
  exactly one clarifying question before assuming.

